WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.250
- I have to ask

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:03.660
because we are a few days
from Valentine's Day.

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.170
So do you and Warren celebrate?

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:06.003
Do y'all?

00:00:06.003 --> 00:00:07.330
'Cause it's been many years, so.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:08.170
- It has been many years.

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.040
So are you like no pressure
kind of Valentine's day?

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:12.880
Or do you still go for it?

00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:14.190
- It's pretty no pressure.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.930
I mean, we are 30 years married

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:18.763
in March.
- Wow.

00:00:18.763 --> 00:00:19.596
(audience applauding)

00:00:19.596 --> 00:00:21.120
- How long have you been together?

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:22.054
- 31.

00:00:22.054 --> 00:00:22.887
- 31, okay.

00:00:22.887 --> 00:00:23.720
Right on, right on.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:24.553
- Yeah.
- That's a lot of years.

00:00:24.553 --> 00:00:25.680
- It's a lot of years.
- Yeah.

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:27.990
- And we're both very proud of that.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:28.823
- [Kelly] I would be too.

00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:29.690
- We have four kids.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.040
I mean, it's a lot of life,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.600
but Valentine's is pretty low key.

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:38.070
He will generally make
me a little Valentine,

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.560
like with just a little red felt pen.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:43.393
- Yeah.

00:00:43.393 --> 00:00:44.226
Make a little heart,

00:00:44.226 --> 00:00:46.327
and he's very economical
(audience laughing)

00:00:46.327 --> 00:00:47.530
in his message.

00:00:47.530 --> 00:00:49.130
- But is it thoughtful though?

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:52.140
'Cause I feel like we can
buy whatever we wanna buy

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:53.230
if we wanna present, you know?

00:00:53.230 --> 00:00:54.900
So I like thoughtful.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:56.027
- Yes, and there's nothing.
- Just so you know.

00:00:56.027 --> 00:00:57.140
You just keep that in your mind.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.650
- There's nothing to buy for him.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.760
He's like one of those men.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.890
You cannot find anything that he-

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:02.723
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:01:02.723 --> 00:01:03.730
- Yeah, it's just he's,

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.440
so no, it's usually something small.

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:06.273
It's a little note.

00:01:06.273 --> 00:01:07.831
It's a flower, it's a-
- I love that.

00:01:07.831 --> 00:01:08.664
- Yeah.

00:01:08.664 --> 00:01:09.620
- I love that.

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.250
30 years, way to go.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.637
(audience applauding)
So what about you?

00:01:12.637 --> 00:01:14.437
You are your wife, what do y'all do?

00:01:15.470 --> 00:01:17.220
- Well, we've been married 18 years,

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.717
so doing really good at that.
- Okay, okay.

00:01:18.717 --> 00:01:19.908
- Not bad, is it?
- 18 years.

00:01:19.908 --> 00:01:20.741
- [Kenneth] Not bad.

00:01:20.741 --> 00:01:21.574
- [Annette] That is not bad.

00:01:21.574 --> 00:01:22.500
- Not bad.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.408
I do bad poetry.

00:01:24.408 --> 00:01:25.650
So that's a...
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.460
No, I mean bad poetry.

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:28.480
And she waits for it every year.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.470
Her eyes roll

00:01:29.470 --> 00:01:30.920
on Valentine's Day morning
(Annette laughing)

00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:31.810
as she opens the thing,

00:01:31.810 --> 00:01:33.747
which usually goes something like,

00:01:33.747 --> 00:01:36.640
"Roses are red, violets are blue.

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:38.432
You need the bathroom, but I use the loo."

00:01:38.432 --> 00:01:39.642
(Annette and Kelly laughing)

00:01:39.642 --> 00:01:41.238
That kind of thing.

00:01:41.238 --> 00:01:43.864
(laughs) I mean, I wish it
were a bit more Shakespearean,

00:01:43.864 --> 00:01:44.870
but that's,
- Oh my god.

00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:45.830
that's as far as I can go.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:48.027
- [Kelly] Oh my god, I love it though.

